    "narrative": "Our offensive outlook for 2026-05-21 centers on exploiting favorable SP_xERA matchups to bolster our efficiency totals. The premier play today is **Geraldo Perdomo** (67.55), who benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Zach Agnos (5.15 xERA). With an elite 19% SP skill adjustment, **Geraldo Perdomo** is the primary driver for our day, followed closely by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.16), whose aggressive placement in the #2 hole and solid park factors offset the presence of Mize. While **Tyler Freeman** (65.99) sits in a strong spot against Rodriguez, his \"Lineup Pending\" status necessitates a slight caution; if he drops out of the #3 spot, we may see a minor regression in his run-scoring potential. \n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved evaluating our outfield depth, as **Lawrence Butler** (54.21) remains our strongest fringe starter. While **Lawrence Butler** suffers from a significant -8% penalty due to his #9 batting position, his massive 13% platoon edge against Soriano was enough to keep him in the lineup over speculative alternatives. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, alongside **Will Smith**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Taylor Ward**, all of whom are unavailable due to team off-days. We are currently carrying a lean active roster; players like **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, and **Matt Chapman** are resting, but we are positioned well to capitalize on the high-probability matchups for **Daulton Varsho** (57.30), whose platoon disadvantage against Rod\u00f3n is mitigated by a favorable park environment.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding **Masyn Winn** (41.87), who is currently our most marginal start. His score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Ashcraft and an elite catcher defense (-1.0%), making him the first candidate to swap if we receive late-breaking lineup news. As we navigate the schedule, keep an eye on our deeper bench assets like **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** should any of today\u2019s starters receive a surprise rest day or weather-related cancellation.",
